From: giuseppegrilli <giugrilli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:48:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable full-display screen sharing through Android MediaProjection

Public Desktop Android builds cancel getDisplayMedia when no service-loaded
picker exists. Offer a full-display fallback through public Android APIs,
with a website disclosure followed by the real MediaProjection consent.

Keep native capture-policy checks, foreground notification and stop paths.
Own one request across Activity recreation and native teardown, transfer the
grant before picker completion, and bound startup waits. An unconsumed native
handoff fails closed until process restart rather than risking grant reuse.

Handle full-display rotation before Android 14 and reject unsupported I420
frames instead of entering the pinned native implementation's NOTIMPLEMENTED
callback. Reports stay local and omit URLs, account data and intent contents.

Only Android 11+ full-display video is supported: no tab picker or system
audio. The existing WINDOW transport can report displaySurface as window.

Update capture unit-test sources and put browser dialog strings in GRIT.
See docs/screen-sharing.md in the Bare repository for validation status and
manual checks. This upstream extraction has not been built or tested.
---
